# REQUIRES: python-api, cuda
# The order of the pair terms of the Python model on a GPU when the
# correction for the dispersion leaves one out (#238): a term whose tail
# diverges before and after one whose tail is integrated, and a tunable of
# the term after it.
# RUN: rm -rf %t && mkdir -p %t
# RUN: %python %S/Inputs/pair_tail_system.py %t 60 60 32 3.7 0.5
# RUN: %mdir_python %S/Inputs/python_pair_order.py %t GPU | FileCheck %s
# CHECK: GPU Double: far, r8 and r8, far give the same potential, virial, pressure and forces
# CHECK: GPU Double: the tail of r8 after far -0.033382762 against its closed form -0.033382762
# CHECK: GPU Double: a tunable c8 of r8 after far gives the program compiled with its value
# CHECK: GPU Mixed: far, r8 and r8, far give the same potential, virial, pressure and forces
# CHECK: GPU Mixed: the tail of r8 after far
# CHECK: GPU Mixed: a tunable c8 of r8 after far gives the program compiled with its value
# CHECK: python pair order passed
